# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# The explicit `eol=lf` (rather than a bare `text=auto`) is deliberate: this
# repo is commonly cloned onto a Windows path that is also reachable from WSL.
# With `core.autocrlf=true`, Windows Git checks files out as CRLF, and Linux
# Git — which defaults to `autocrlf=false` — then reports every one of them as
# modified. Pinning the working-tree ending makes both agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception: some constructs break unless the
# file is CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never diff or line-ending-normalize these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
